description: Keep pages and route routers thin — extract into feature/cron/oauth modules
alwaysApply: true
---

Modularization (post-2026-07 split):

## File budgets (enforced by `npm run check:structure`)
- Page gods stay composition-focused: Messages/Content/Ecommerce/Calendar under their budgets
- `server/routes/oauthRoutes.ts` and `server/routes/cronRoutes.js` are **wiring only**

## Where new code goes
- **Cron jobs:** `server/routes/cron/<job>.js` exporting `registerXCron(app, deps)` — then call it from `cronRoutes.js`. Never add `app.get("/api/cron/...")` inline in `cronRoutes.js`.
- **OAuth platforms:** `server/routes/oauth/<platform>OAuthRoutes.ts` exporting `registerXOAuthRoutes` — then call from `oauthRoutes.ts`. Never add `app.get("/api/auth/...")` inline in `oauthRoutes.ts`.
- **Page UI/logic:** `src/features/<area>/` components, hooks, helpers. Pages own composition + wiring only.
- **Provider APIs:** `server/providers/` — keep provider-specific fetch/token logic out of routes/UI.

## Tests
- Prefer Vitest unit tests of pure helpers and registration smoke tests (`src/test/routeRegistration.test.ts`).
- Do not invent a full Express/supertest harness unless product explicitly needs HTTP contract tests.
- When adding a Vercel cron in `vercel.json`, ensure a cron module registers that exact path (CI checks this).

## Docs
- Structural changes update `ai/ARCHITECTURE.md` and/or `ai/DECISIONS.md` as part of done.
